{
  "id": "noise_generated_in_air_ducts",
  "title": "Noise Generated in Air Ducts",
  "description": "Calculate the sound power level generated by air flow in ducts based on air velocity and duct cross-sectional area using empirical equations.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "content": "Air Duct Noise Calculation",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "velocity",
          "label": "Air Velocity",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 10,
          "unit": "m/s"
        },
        {
          "id": "area",
          "label": "Duct Cross-Sectional Area",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.0314,
          "unit": "m²"
        },
        {
          "id": "unit_system",
          "label": "Unit System",
          "type": "select",
          "defaultValue": "metric",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "Metric (m/s, m²)",
              "value": "metric"
            },
            {
              "label": "Imperial (ft/min, in²)",
              "value": "imperial"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "sound_power_level",
          "label": "Sound Power Level (LN)",
          "formula": "inputs.unit_system === 'metric' ? 10 + 50 * Math.log10(inputs.velocity) + 10 * Math.log10(inputs.area) : 10 + 50 * Math.log10(inputs.velocity / 197) + 10 * Math.log10(inputs.area / 1550)",
          "unit": "dB",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Parameter",
        "Metric Value",
        "Imperial Value",
        "Unit"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Air Velocity (Example 1)",
          "10",
          "3280.84",
          "m/s / ft/min"
        ],
        [
          "Duct Area (Example 1)",
          "0.0314",
          "48.63",
          "m² / in²"
        ],
        [
          "Sound Power Level (Example 1)",
          "45",
          "45",
          "dB"
        ],
        [
          "Air Velocity (Example 2)",
          "20",
          "6561.68",
          "m/s / ft/min"
        ],
        [
          "Duct Area (Example 2)",
          "0.0314",
          "48.63",
          "m² / in²"
        ],
        [
          "Sound Power Level (Example 2)",
          "60",
          "60",
          "dB"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Calculation Formula\n\n**Metric Units:**\n\nLN = 10 + 50 log(v) + 10 log(A)\n\nWhere:\n- LN = Sound power level in the duct (dB)\n- v = Air velocity (m/s)\n- A = Air duct cross-sectional area (m²)\n\n**Imperial Units:**\n\nLN = 10 + 50 log(vi / 197) + 10 log(Ai / 1550)\n\nWhere:\n- vi = Air velocity (ft/min)\n- Ai = Cross-sectional area (in²)\n\n## Notes\n\n- Due to noise generated by fans, noise generated inside ducts by air flow can generally be neglected in practice.\n- The calculation uses empirical equations based on experimental data.\n- For circular ducts, cross-sectional area A = π × (d/2)², where d is the diameter."
    }
  ]
}